{"name":"Goldvreneli 1882","hex":"#e7de54","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Vreneli","blocks":[{"text":"Vreneli is the informal name for a range of legal tender gold coins of the Swiss franc. The coins were issued between 1897 and 1936, in 1947 and in 1949. All coins issued after 1936 are restrikes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/20_Schweizer_Franken_Goldvreneli.png/330px-20_Schweizer_Franken_Goldvreneli.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vreneli","wikidata":"Q667160"},{"title":"1882","blocks":[{"text":"1882 (MDCCCLXXXII) was a common year starting on Sunday of the Gregorian calendar and a common year starting on Friday of the Julian calendar, the 1882nd year of the Common Era (CE) and Anno Domini (AD) designations, the 882nd year of the 2nd millennium, the 82nd year of the 19th century, and the 3rd year of the 1880s decade. As of the start of 1882, the Gregorian calendar was 12 days ahead of the Julian calendar, which remained in localized use until 1923."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/First_Trolleybuss_of_Siemens_in_Berlin_1882_%28postcard%29.jpg/330px-First_Trolleybuss_of_Siemens_in_Berlin_1882_%28postcard%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1882","wikidata":"Q7812"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/20_Schweizer_Franken_Goldvrenzeli_Wertseite.png/500px-20_Schweizer_Franken_Goldvrenzeli_Wertseite.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/20_Schweizer_Franken_Goldvrenzeli_Wertseite.png/500px-20_Schweizer_Franken_Goldvrenzeli_Wertseite.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3